course: dictionary
lesson: 13660
title: Inflow: things coming in
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An inflow is something flowing or coming into a place. The word in- means into, and flow means to move steadily, like water. «The inflow of water from the river filled the lake after the heavy rain.» The water is moving into the lake, so inflow means water flowing in.
explain: Inflow has an opposite: outflow, which means flowing out. «The tank had an inflow from the pipe and an outflow through the tap.» If more water flows in than flows out, the tank fills up. Looking at the opposite word can help you work out what a new word means.
explain: Inflow is not only about water. People, money and goods can have an inflow too. «The shop saw an inflow of customers before the holidays.» Here the customers are coming into the shop, so inflow means arrival.
fact: Inflow means the movement of water, air or other things flowing into a place.
fact: Inflow can also mean the arrival of money, people or goods into a place.
fact: Outflow is the opposite: things flowing out of a place.
fact: Cash inflow means money coming in, such as the money a shop takes in.
fact: Useful phrases: inflow and outflow, inflow of water, an inflow of visitors.
exercise: «The inflow of water from the river filled the lake after the rain.» What does inflow mean here? | Rain falling on the hills | A boat sailing across the lake | Water flowing out of the lake | *Water flowing into the lake
exercise: Find the word that is the opposite of inflow in «The tank had an inflow from the pipe and an outflow through the tap.» | *outflow | tank | pipe | inflow
exercise: «The shop saw an inflow of customers before the holidays.» What does inflow mean here? | People leaving the shop | A sign on the shop door | *People arriving at the shop | Goods sent back to the factory
test: «Each week the bank counts the cash inflow and the cash outflow.» What is cash inflow? | Coins that are very old | *Money coming in | Cash lost in the post | Money going out
test: Maya says a tank with a big inflow and a small outflow will fill up. Is Maya right? | *Yes, more water comes in than goes out | No, the tank can never fill up | Yes, because the tank is made of glass | No, the outflow always fills the tank
exam: What does «an inflow of tourists» mean? | A map of the town | *Many tourists arriving in a place | Many tourists leaving a place | A tourist who lost a bag
